WEBVTT

00:00.660 --> 00:04.400
<i>The finals of the Shizuoka prefecture had finally started.</i>

00:04.400 --> 00:05.840
<i>Just as the match started,</i>

00:05.840 --> 00:09.030
<i>the ball was stolen by the Otomo Quartet.</i>

00:09.030 --> 00:13.990
<i>They passed the ball to Nitta, but Tsubasa stood in his way.</i>

00:13.990 --> 00:18.530
<i>An 'ace vs. ace' showdown erupts early in the match!</i>

00:18.530 --> 00:22.500
<i>After a tight clash, with Tsubasa taking the ball after struggling,</i>

00:22.500 --> 00:27.920
<i>his attacks are shut down by the Quartet and its dogged defense.</i>

00:27.920 --> 00:31.380
This match could end with Nankatsu losing, y'know.

00:31.380 --> 00:38.480
<i>As Nagasaki representative Hiroshi Jito and Katagiri from the Japanese National Football Federation foresee a possible loss for Nankatsu,</i>

00:38.480 --> 00:43.560
<i>Nitta tries to make that prediction into reality, and performs his Falcon Shot.</i>

00:43.560 --> 00:47.310
Take this! Falcon Shot!

00:53.700 --> 00:56.180
<i>Despite not making it into the goal, Tsubasa,</i>

00:56.180 --> 01:00.870
<i>feeling the power of the shot first-hand, was fired up.</i>

01:00.870 --> 01:04.710
Non-Trap Running Volley!

01:07.780 --> 01:11.960
<i>Tsubasa scores a magnificent goal to open the score!</i>

01:11.960 --> 01:14.050
<i>Ending the first half on a 1-0 score,</i>

01:14.050 --> 01:17.310
<i>the match moves into to its turbulent second half!</i>

01:18.140 --> 01:20.180
DRESSING ROOM A
NANKATSU MIDDLE SCHOOL - WAITING ROOM

01:18.700 --> 01:21.360
All right, everybody did a good job.

01:22.180 --> 01:23.980
Coach, what's that?

01:23.980 --> 01:27.370
Our Manager's hand-made lemon slices in honey.

01:27.370 --> 01:30.510
Oh yeah! That's generous of her.

01:31.400 --> 01:33.400
Keep this up in the second half too.

01:33.400 --> 01:35.030
Yes, sir!

01:35.660 --> 01:39.200
I'm sorry. I wasn't able to protect our goal.

01:39.200 --> 01:42.490
No, it's not just your fault.

01:42.490 --> 01:45.330
It's true that Tsubasa is a level above the rest.

01:45.330 --> 01:48.790
Damn it! I couldn't even score one goal.

01:48.790 --> 01:51.040
Don't panic, Nitta.

01:51.040 --> 01:54.050
They'll come at us the same way they did in the first half.

01:54.050 --> 01:56.050
We'll also do the same.

01:56.050 --> 02:00.090
We defend and you score, that's how Otomo is.

02:00.090 --> 02:02.060
This is our best and only option.

02:02.060 --> 02:04.220
We're counting on you, Nitta.

02:04.220 --> 02:05.500
Yes.

02:06.390 --> 02:09.390
<i>But as I've discovered this first half,</i>

02:09.390 --> 02:13.020
<i>I can't dribble past Tsubasa in a one-on-one.</i>

02:13.610 --> 02:15.780
<i>So, what can I do?</i>

02:17.620 --> 02:18.740
<i>If...</i>

02:29.270 --> 02:31.980
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:29.270 --> 02:31.980
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:32.900 --> 02:35.570
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:32.900 --> 02:35.570
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:36.490 --> 02:39.200
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

02:36.490 --> 02:39.200
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

02:46.070 --> 02:48.890
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

02:46.070 --> 02:48.890
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

02:48.890 --> 02:55.170
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

02:48.890 --> 02:55.170
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

02:55.170 --> 03:01.050
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

02:55.170 --> 03:01.050
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

03:01.050 --> 03:07.640
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

03:01.050 --> 03:07.640
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

03:07.640 --> 03:11.650
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

03:07.640 --> 03:11.650
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

03:11.650 --> 03:16.150
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

03:11.650 --> 03:16.150
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

03:16.150 --> 03:21.700
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

03:16.150 --> 03:21.700
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

03:21.700 --> 03:23.280
<i>baka darou?</i>

03:21.700 --> 03:23.280
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

03:23.280 --> 03:24.490
<i>ai</i>

03:23.280 --> 03:24.490
<i>Love!</i>

03:24.490 --> 03:28.120
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

03:24.490 --> 03:28.120
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

03:28.120 --> 03:37.880
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

03:28.120 --> 03:37.880
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

03:37.880 --> 03:38.690
<i>ai</i>

03:37.880 --> 03:38.690
<i>Love!</i>

03:38.690 --> 03:42.490
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

03:38.690 --> 03:42.490
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

03:42.490 --> 03:46.490
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

03:42.490 --> 03:46.490
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

03:46.490 --> 03:52.750
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

03:46.490 --> 03:52.750
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

03:52.750 --> 03:55.560
<i>hanasanai</i>

03:52.750 --> 03:55.560
<i>for a single moment!</i>

03:57.420 --> 04:01.760
<b><b>EPISODE 31:
FALCON VS. TSUBASA</b></b>

03:59.600 --> 04:03.160
<i>The awaited second half of action begins, and 30 minutes remain.</i>

04:03.160 --> 04:04.300
<i>There's no choice.</i>

04:04.300 --> 04:05.130
Let's go!

04:05.130 --> 04:08.060
With them being behind, they're fired up now!

04:08.060 --> 04:09.990
Stay sharp and move!

04:09.990 --> 04:10.770
Yeah!

04:10.770 --> 04:12.310
<i>There's no other choice!</i>

04:12.310 --> 04:16.040
<i>Can Otomo Middle School turn the score around this half?</i>

04:16.560 --> 04:20.070
<i>Nitta runs towards the goal.</i>

04:20.070 --> 04:22.860
<i>But this strategy hasn't worked that well so far for them.</i>

04:22.860 --> 04:24.610
It's on, Nitta.

04:24.610 --> 04:28.240
<i>Because Nankatsu's ace Tsubasa continues to personally mark him.</i>

04:29.420 --> 04:30.750
<i>Damn you, Tsubasa!</i>

04:30.750 --> 04:34.370
<i>But regardless, we will still pass to Nitta!</i>

04:35.630 --> 04:39.170
<i>With my speed, I can outrun his mark.</i>

04:41.020 --> 04:44.090
<i>But, if I trap the ball, I won't have a chance to shoot...</i>

04:52.010 --> 04:55.980
<i>Oh! Did Nitta try to shoot without trapping the ball?</i>

04:55.980 --> 05:00.940
<i>But his timing is off, and the ball flies out of bounds.</i>

05:00.940 --> 05:01.690
Nitta!

05:01.690 --> 05:02.820
Nitta!

05:02.820 --> 05:06.200
Hey, hey! It's impossible for you to move like Tsubasa!

05:06.200 --> 05:09.280
You're 10 years too early to be trying that shot!

05:10.650 --> 05:15.280
<i>I know that. I know that better than all of you think you do.</i>

05:15.280 --> 05:20.920
<i>But this is the only way to be able to score against Nankatsu. Against Tsubasa.</i>

05:20.920 --> 05:27.010
What's up with him? Trying a high level shot he's never practiced.

05:27.010 --> 05:28.200
I don't know.

05:28.200 --> 05:30.930
But, no matter what, we will pass the ball to him.

05:30.930 --> 05:32.580
There's nothing else we can do!

05:34.930 --> 05:38.520
<i>Nankatsu's Taki resumes the match with a throw-in.</i>

05:40.460 --> 05:41.940
Iwami!

05:43.360 --> 05:44.110
I got it!

05:44.110 --> 05:44.820
Nishio!

05:44.820 --> 05:47.660
<i>Otomo with a swift interception!</i>

05:47.660 --> 05:50.580
<i>The second half has lit a fire inside Otomo's players.</i>

05:50.580 --> 05:51.320
All right!

05:51.320 --> 05:53.950
<i>Niita speeds up to break away from his mark!</i>

05:53.950 --> 05:54.910
Nitta!

05:55.830 --> 05:58.920
<i>Nitta and the Otomo Quartet are syncing together perfectly!</i>

06:03.340 --> 06:06.970
<i>Again, Nitta tries a forceful non-trap shot!</i>

06:06.970 --> 06:08.600
<i>But once again, it was in vain.</i>

06:08.600 --> 06:10.220
<i>It might be too hard for him.</i>

06:10.940 --> 06:15.640
<i>Despite Nitta's pedigree, a difficult skill like a non-trap shot</i>

06:15.640 --> 06:17.890
<i>might be too much to ask from a middle schooler.</i>

06:17.890 --> 06:19.720
Nitta.

06:19.720 --> 06:20.900
This guy...

06:20.900 --> 06:22.610
Now we can't predict how it will end!

06:23.760 --> 06:24.860
How what will end?

06:25.300 --> 06:29.470
The timing of that shot was far better than the first.

06:29.490 --> 06:32.780
There's the distinct possibility that before this half ends...

06:32.780 --> 06:34.780
There's no other choice...

06:34.780 --> 06:36.970
To use the long pass that goes over you...

06:36.970 --> 06:40.280
I must perfect this, my Non-Trap Running Volley Falcon Shot.

06:40.280 --> 06:44.050
I have no other choice but to do it!

06:44.820 --> 06:47.920
<i>Otomo cuts another pass!</i>

06:47.920 --> 06:50.760
<i>And a long pass is sent forward again to Nitta!</i>

06:50.760 --> 06:55.100
<i>Being marked by Tsubasa, Nitta uses his speed to create separation.</i>

06:55.100 --> 06:56.680
<i>The main point is in the timing!</i>

06:57.810 --> 06:59.280
<i>This time, for sure...!</i>

07:02.550 --> 07:04.320
<i>He goes for a direct shot!</i>

07:08.240 --> 07:09.930
<i>Oh no, it barely misses!</i>

07:09.930 --> 07:13.030
<i>After three diligent tries to score a straight goal,</i>

07:13.030 --> 07:14.490
<i>he's blown them all!</i>

07:14.490 --> 07:16.850
<i>I'm not wrong!</i>

07:16.850 --> 07:21.500
<i>Nitta's timing on these shots keeps improving.</i>

07:21.500 --> 07:24.500
<i>If this keeps going, it could spell disaster.</i>

07:24.500 --> 07:27.510
<i>You're one hell of a guy, Shun Nitta.</i>

07:27.510 --> 07:31.220
<i>In a limited time, and within a match,</i>

07:31.220 --> 07:34.390
<i>he's been working to master that shot.</i>

07:34.800 --> 07:35.970
<i>He might be rough,</i>

07:35.970 --> 07:40.020
<i>but he has a wonderful instinct for football.</i>

07:40.020 --> 07:46.770
<i>And thanks to the Otomo Quartet's efforts, Nankatsu's offense has been completely shut down.</i>

07:46.770 --> 07:50.440
<i>As a result, Tsubasa was supposed to be in the defensive half of the team,</i>

07:50.440 --> 07:54.700
<i>yet he's been able to do nothing but mark Nitta.</i>

07:54.700 --> 07:57.450
<i>Even with the lead in Nankatsu's hands,</i>

07:57.450 --> 07:59.750
<i>they're the ones constantly being pushed.</i>

08:00.220 --> 08:05.750
<i>If Nitta somehow manages to master that shot,</i>

08:05.750 --> 08:08.840
<i>Nankatsu's victory will fall apart.</i>

08:08.840 --> 08:11.960
I hate that Nitta guy.

08:13.260 --> 08:15.760
Calm down, Kumi.

08:15.760 --> 08:18.640
What do you mean, "calm down"?

08:18.640 --> 08:20.660
He keeps getting past Tsubasa's mark,

08:20.660 --> 08:22.140
and that's pissing me off!

08:22.140 --> 08:24.600
Don't you think so too, Sanae?

08:24.600 --> 08:26.870
Well, that's just how a match is.

08:26.870 --> 08:29.750
Sanae, you are just too sympathetic.

08:29.750 --> 08:35.570
They'll be fine. Tsubasa and the others.

08:37.490 --> 08:39.820
Isn't Nankatsu passionate?

08:39.820 --> 08:41.930
Y-yeah...

08:41.930 --> 08:44.670
I'm not jealous or anything, y'know!

08:44.670 --> 08:49.830
But even though Otomo has Nankatsu's offense shut down,

08:49.830 --> 08:52.460
the fact that they only have Nitta on offense is sad.

08:52.460 --> 08:56.180
If someone else could join Nitta on offense, then by now,

08:56.180 --> 08:58.280
they'd have probably scored three times.

08:58.280 --> 09:02.060
Unsurprisingly, it just shows the team power required for football.

09:02.060 --> 09:10.020
Yeah. And team power is something that we, Toho Academy, excel in.

09:10.620 --> 09:12.970
That's why, even if Nankatsu has Tsubasa,

09:12.970 --> 09:17.740
we will be the ones to conquer the nationals this year.

09:20.240 --> 09:21.160
What?

09:21.160 --> 09:25.640
<i>Nankatsu's captain Tsubasa, who had been doggedly marking Nitta the entire time,</i>

09:25.640 --> 09:27.830
<i>goes on the attack for the first time this half!</i>

09:27.830 --> 09:32.580
<i>To stop these passes from constantly being sent to Nitta, I have no choice but to attack.</i>

09:32.580 --> 09:35.970
<i>Also, we desperately need to score another goal to stay safe.</i>

09:36.530 --> 09:37.300
He's here!

09:37.300 --> 09:38.300
Tsubasa!

09:38.300 --> 09:42.180
<i>He dribbles past the opponent's midfield!</i>

09:42.180 --> 09:44.080
All right, keep going Tsubasa!

09:44.080 --> 09:46.310
This is the usual Nankatsu!

09:47.600 --> 09:48.440
Take that!

09:48.440 --> 09:50.150
<i>Tsubasa, instead of pushing through,</i>

09:50.150 --> 09:51.650
<i>sends the ball to the right!</i>

09:52.160 --> 09:53.820
<i>The ball is for Taki!</i>

09:57.420 --> 09:58.070
Taki!

09:58.070 --> 10:02.790
We're all too familiar with your touchline dribble and centering strategy!

10:02.790 --> 10:05.120
Well, you never know what else may come.

10:05.610 --> 10:06.410
What?!

10:06.410 --> 10:08.170
All right! Good work, Taki!

10:08.170 --> 10:11.050
<i>Taki, instead of moving up the sidelines,</i>

10:11.050 --> 10:12.500
<i>cuts towards the goal!</i>

10:13.880 --> 10:15.260
I'm counting on you, Kisugi!

10:17.320 --> 10:18.680
All right! I've got it!

10:18.680 --> 10:20.180
<i>It's in front of the goal!</i>

10:20.180 --> 10:21.050
Come!

10:21.050 --> 10:22.680
<i>Kisugi shoots!</i>

10:26.120 --> 10:29.650
<i>Oh, it's been caught! The keeper makes a fine play!</i>

10:29.650 --> 10:31.400
Nice catch, Ichijo!

10:31.400 --> 10:35.690
<i>Nankatsu's first chance in the second half ends in failure!</i>

10:36.330 --> 10:37.150
Take that!

10:38.380 --> 10:41.160
Damn it! And we attacked well, there...

10:41.160 --> 10:43.140
<i>When Tsubasa goes into offense,</i>

10:43.140 --> 10:46.160
<i>a rhythm forms in between the players.</i>

10:46.160 --> 10:51.080
<i>But Otomo swiftly goes on the counter attack!</i>

10:51.080 --> 10:52.880
Take that, Nitta!

10:55.190 --> 10:57.010
<i>Get the timing right!</i>

10:57.790 --> 11:01.100
<i>Timing! Timing!</i>

11:03.560 --> 11:06.100
<i>Oh, the timing feels right!</i>

11:06.100 --> 11:06.720
<i>This is bad!</i>

11:12.600 --> 11:14.690
<i>Oh no! It hit his hand!</i>

11:15.780 --> 11:18.760
<i>Nankatsu's defender Oda is called for a hand ball!</i>

11:18.760 --> 11:20.570
Oh, man.

11:20.570 --> 11:22.240
This is a chance!

11:22.600 --> 11:25.490
<i>Nitta seemed to be about 80% right on the timing.</i>

11:26.130 --> 11:27.800
<i>But the ball swerved to the right,</i>

11:27.800 --> 11:30.750
<i>and this hit Oda squarely in the arm!</i>

11:30.750 --> 11:32.830
<i>Nankatsu's in a pinch!</i>

11:32.830 --> 11:35.920
<i>This is a chance for a direct free kick!</i>

11:36.350 --> 11:40.930
<i>All right! I can go for a Falcon Shot without anyone marking me!</i>

11:41.450 --> 11:44.970
<i>Nitta... Surely, he'll directly go for goal, here.</i>

11:47.180 --> 11:49.080
Don't leave any wide gaps!

11:49.080 --> 11:52.740
Everybody, get a lot more closer! Don't let anything through!

11:52.740 --> 11:53.350
Yeah!

11:55.460 --> 11:57.680
<i>The front wall will block his path.</i>

11:57.680 --> 11:59.530
<i>The left is covered by Morisaki,</i>

11:59.530 --> 12:01.990
<i>and I'm covering the right side.</i>

12:01.990 --> 12:06.120
Tsubasa, maybe Nitta will try a pass instead of shooting.

12:06.120 --> 12:09.540
No, I'm sure he'll attempt to shoot on goal.

12:10.280 --> 12:12.000
I'm counting on you, Nitta.

12:12.000 --> 12:13.620
Yes.

12:13.620 --> 12:18.910
<i>Will Otomo bet on Nitta's shooting,</i>

12:18.910 --> 12:21.470
<i>or will they come up with a different plan?</i>

12:23.090 --> 12:24.080
Let's go!

12:24.080 --> 12:26.350
<i>Oh! Urabe runs forward to the ball!</i>

12:26.350 --> 12:27.180
What?

12:27.180 --> 12:28.200
Nitta!

12:28.200 --> 12:29.140
<i>He does not shoot!</i>

12:29.140 --> 12:31.480
<i>As expected, Nitta takes the kick!</i>

12:31.480 --> 12:35.150
<i>Eat this! Falcon Shot!</i>

12:45.680 --> 12:46.450
Eat this!

12:48.660 --> 12:51.040
Falcon Shot!

12:53.640 --> 12:56.670
<i>Nitta shoots straight ahead!</i>

12:57.330 --> 12:58.460
We blocked it!

12:58.460 --> 12:59.670
That's it!

12:59.670 --> 13:02.880
<i>But that hit has opened a hole in Nankatsu's wall!</i>

13:02.880 --> 13:04.930
<i>Crap! Was that what he was after?!</i>

13:04.930 --> 13:05.860
You did it!

13:05.860 --> 13:07.430
Go, Nitta!

13:08.430 --> 13:09.770
I've got this!

13:10.760 --> 13:12.060
I won't let you score!

13:12.060 --> 13:12.810
Go!

13:14.480 --> 13:15.190
That move...!

13:15.890 --> 13:17.730
Take my second Falcon Shot!

13:19.710 --> 13:21.700
<i>Tsubasa clears it with his head!</i>

13:21.700 --> 13:22.720
Tsubasa!

13:22.720 --> 13:23.570
What?!

13:23.570 --> 13:25.810
<i>Otomo Middle School still couldn't score!</i>

13:25.810 --> 13:27.950
That was Wakashimazu's move!

13:33.380 --> 13:35.250
Nice clear, Tsubasa!

13:35.250 --> 13:38.000
Your defensive skills are also great, Tsubasa Ozora.

13:38.000 --> 13:39.220
Great!

13:39.220 --> 13:41.750
Tsubasa is just so cool.

13:42.440 --> 13:44.040
It can't be...

13:44.040 --> 13:46.760
My Falcon Shot...

13:46.760 --> 13:49.160
That shot was perfect.

13:49.160 --> 13:50.550
How could he block it?

13:50.550 --> 13:51.820
All right.

13:51.820 --> 13:53.640
Otomo is discouraged.

13:53.640 --> 13:54.730
It's up to you, Izawa!

13:54.730 --> 13:56.140
Get that ball!

13:56.140 --> 13:56.980
Got it!

13:57.480 --> 13:58.600
Crap! Fall back!

13:58.600 --> 14:01.730
<i>Tsubasa goes on the offensive without a moment's delay!</i>

14:01.730 --> 14:05.400
Nakao! Hiraoka! Don't let Nankatsu get that ball!

14:06.050 --> 14:09.160
I won't lose a heading showdown!

14:09.160 --> 14:10.390
Tsubasa!

14:10.390 --> 14:12.410
<i>Izawa wins the matchup!</i>

14:13.080 --> 14:14.410
Nice, Izawa!

14:14.410 --> 14:16.910
<i>With this, Tsubasa goes on the attack!</i>

14:16.910 --> 14:18.430
All right! Let's do this!

14:18.430 --> 14:20.430
<i>They're emulating Otomo's play style!</i>

14:20.430 --> 14:22.710
<i>This is Nankatsu's counter attack!</i>

14:22.710 --> 14:24.380
Get back guys, hurry up!

14:24.380 --> 14:26.100
Go, Tsubasa!

14:26.100 --> 14:28.630
Keep running straight to the goal like that!

14:28.630 --> 14:30.890
<i>If we concede a goal now and fall 2 goals behind,</i>

14:30.890 --> 14:32.890
<i>we'll have no shot left at winning!</i>

14:32.890 --> 14:35.810
<i>But if I can just somehow steal the ball from Tsubasa now,</i>

14:35.810 --> 14:37.380
<i>there's no one marking Nitta...!</i>

14:37.380 --> 14:40.900
<i>I can turn this absolute crisis into an absolute chance!</i>

14:40.900 --> 14:42.190
Urabe...

14:42.190 --> 14:44.610
Make sure to get that ball from Tsubasa!

14:44.610 --> 14:45.440
Yeah!

14:45.440 --> 14:47.590
<i>Tsubasa's attack is fast.</i>

14:47.590 --> 14:51.030
<i>Only Otomo's Quartet has been able to keep up with his speed!</i>

14:51.640 --> 14:53.030
<i>This time for sure...</i>

14:53.030 --> 14:54.830
Tsubasa...

14:54.830 --> 14:56.330
<i>I'll break through!</i>

14:56.330 --> 14:58.330
We'll stop him! I'll go first!

14:59.080 --> 15:02.290
<i>Tsubasa flings the ball with a chip kick!</i>

15:02.290 --> 15:03.170
What?!

15:03.170 --> 15:06.340
<i>He gets past Kishida who was the closest to him!</i>

15:06.340 --> 15:07.560
You won't go any further!

15:07.560 --> 15:08.970
I'm next!

15:09.480 --> 15:12.430
<i>He deftly avoids his second opponent!</i>

15:12.430 --> 15:13.720
Tsubasa...!

15:13.720 --> 15:16.220
<i>Will he be able to evade a third opponent from above?</i>

15:16.220 --> 15:17.680
Like hell I'd let you!

15:19.270 --> 15:20.270
What?!

15:20.270 --> 15:21.770
<i>He dribbles past the third from below!</i>

15:21.770 --> 15:25.860
<i>With a snap judgment, Tsubasa grounds the ball and sends it just ahead, breaking free!</i>

15:25.860 --> 15:29.740
<i>Damn you, Tsubasa, it's in this kind of
moment that you really work your magic.</i>

15:29.740 --> 15:31.070
Just one more...

15:31.070 --> 15:34.950
<i>Urabe is challenging Tsubasa to the loose ball!</i>

15:34.950 --> 15:36.030
Captain!

15:38.040 --> 15:40.580
<i>A tenacious sliding tackle from Urabe!</i>

15:40.580 --> 15:42.040
<i>They get there simultaneously!</i>

15:42.490 --> 15:46.040
<i>The ball is deflected up into the air, as though possessed!</i>

15:46.040 --> 15:46.800
All right!

15:47.340 --> 15:49.800
<i>Tsubasa runs to where the ball is falling!</i>

15:52.340 --> 15:52.960
<i>Damn it!</i>

15:52.960 --> 15:54.390
<i>We'll definitely stop him!</i>

15:54.510 --> 15:56.640
<i>We can't let him shoot!</i>

15:56.760 --> 15:59.020
<i>It will be the end for us if he scores now!</i>

16:00.430 --> 16:02.600
<i>A final effort from the Otomo Quartet!</i>

16:02.600 --> 16:05.080
<i>However, Tsubasa's shot is faster than they are!</i>

16:05.080 --> 16:08.230
<i>His golden right leg breaks free just a second faster!</i>

16:08.230 --> 16:09.110
Ichijo!

16:09.110 --> 16:10.240
It's up to you now!

16:12.760 --> 16:13.770
<i>He got it!</i>

16:13.770 --> 16:15.950
<i>A diving catch from Ichijo!</i>

16:16.830 --> 16:17.840
He did it!

16:17.840 --> 16:18.950
That was cool, Ichijo!

16:19.580 --> 16:21.290
<i>They barely got to it, didn't they?</i>

16:21.540 --> 16:24.700
<i>When the Otomo Quartet went to stop Tsubasa's shot,</i>

16:24.700 --> 16:28.050
<i>for just a split second, their feet managed to touch the ball.</i>

16:28.300 --> 16:31.840
<i>That's how they managed to weaken Tsubasa's shot.</i>

16:31.840 --> 16:34.590
That's what you'd call Otomo Middle School's ferocity, y'know.

16:34.590 --> 16:39.600
<i>Otomo Middle School used the full extent of their defense's power to block Tsubasa's attack!</i>

16:39.600 --> 16:41.300
Oh, come on...

16:41.300 --> 16:43.320
That was unfortunate. Right, Sanae?

16:43.320 --> 16:45.320
We still have plenty of time.

16:45.320 --> 16:48.270
I know, right. And we are in the lead.

16:48.270 --> 16:50.280
But we mustn't let our guards down!

16:50.280 --> 16:52.900
You don't know what will happen till the end.

16:52.900 --> 16:54.410
Come on, Ichijo!

16:54.410 --> 16:55.700
This is our chance!

16:55.700 --> 16:56.490
Okay!

16:57.910 --> 16:58.950
Oh no!

16:58.950 --> 17:01.520
<i>Ichijo sends the ball to Urabe...</i>

17:04.700 --> 17:05.460
Nitta!

17:06.710 --> 17:08.690
<i>...and he sends it to Nitta, who's wide open!</i>

17:08.690 --> 17:10.900
<i>The predicament's turned into a big chance!</i>

17:10.900 --> 17:13.010
<i>They are sure to score if Nitta can get to this.</i>

17:13.010 --> 17:15.590
<i>Tsubasa's won't be back to mark him in time!</i>

17:15.590 --> 17:16.350
We did it!

17:16.350 --> 17:17.660
We'll finally score one!

17:17.660 --> 17:18.720
It's all you, Nitta!

17:18.720 --> 17:20.600
You can make it even if you trap the ball.

17:22.220 --> 17:23.640
<i>Ichijo...</i>

17:23.640 --> 17:25.530
<i>and everyone...</i>

17:25.530 --> 17:28.530
<i>I'm grateful to you for stopping that last attack...</i>

17:28.530 --> 17:32.470
<i>However, even though I'm unmarked,
I won't let this ball touch the ground.</i>

17:32.470 --> 17:34.490
<i>I'll directly score one!</i>

17:38.130 --> 17:40.270
Nitta!

17:40.990 --> 17:41.740
Go!

17:41.740 --> 17:45.580
Non-Trap Running Volley Falcon Shot for you!

17:48.780 --> 17:51.030
<i>It's in! Goal!</i>

17:51.030 --> 17:52.300
<i>They are tied!</i>

17:52.960 --> 17:57.240
<i>Goalkeeper Morisaki and Nankatsu's defenders couldn't do so much as react!</i>

17:57.240 --> 17:58.970
A-amazing...

17:59.900 --> 18:01.370
He got that one in...

18:01.370 --> 18:03.790
What will we do? The score's tied.

18:09.580 --> 18:11.960
I did it...

18:11.960 --> 18:13.130
I did it!

18:13.130 --> 18:14.940
I have finally mastered it!

18:14.940 --> 18:18.070
My Non-Trap Running Volley Falcon Shot!

18:18.070 --> 18:19.820
That bastard...

18:19.820 --> 18:21.580
You finally did it!

18:21.580 --> 18:26.830
<i>In the 10th minute of the second half, Otomo Middle School finally tie the score at 1-1.</i>

18:26.830 --> 18:28.920
Go, go, Otomo!

18:28.920 --> 18:30.720
You were great, Nitta!

18:30.720 --> 18:32.140
We'll get the lead, just like that!

18:32.140 --> 18:36.760
Now, even if Tsubasa's marking him, we can score so long as we get the ball to Nitta!

18:36.760 --> 18:38.400
Keep scoring, Nitta!

18:38.400 --> 18:41.540
<i>Otomo Middle Schhol is fired up after catching up to Nankatsu.</i>

18:41.540 --> 18:44.390
<i>The match has suddenly become very interesting!</i>

18:44.390 --> 18:47.500
<i>Nitta... What a guy you are...!</i>

18:47.500 --> 18:48.940
Damn it!

18:48.940 --> 18:51.310
It's not like we've lost yet.

18:51.310 --> 18:53.600
That's right! The real match starts now!

18:53.600 --> 18:56.320
Stop acting like you've won, Otomo!

18:56.320 --> 18:59.300
Yeah! We're aiming for our third consecutive win at the Nationals!

18:59.300 --> 19:01.490
Like hell we'd lose here!

19:01.490 --> 19:03.620
Tsubasa, let's go for the counter attack!

19:04.640 --> 19:05.830
Guys...

19:05.830 --> 19:09.540
Okay! If they score on you, you score back! That's the basic principle of football!

19:09.540 --> 19:10.660
Let's go, guys!

19:10.660 --> 19:11.960
Yeah!

19:11.960 --> 19:14.180
Nankatsu refuse to lose, right?

19:14.180 --> 19:18.260
Of course they do. It starts for real now. Isn't that right, Sanae?

19:18.260 --> 19:19.470
Yeah.

19:19.470 --> 19:22.320
<i>It's a tie. What will you do, Tsubasa?</i>

19:22.320 --> 19:24.720
<i>Will you keep marking Nitta like you've done so far?</i>

19:24.720 --> 19:25.970
<i>Or will you...</i>

19:25.970 --> 19:27.680
<i>If they score against you, you score back.</i>

19:27.680 --> 19:30.980
<i>Nitta, this time I'll go and score one against you!</i>

19:30.980 --> 19:34.230
Guys, don't you lose in spirit.

19:34.230 --> 19:38.240
<i>Nankatsu prepare their counter attack as their opponent's caught up!</i>

19:38.240 --> 19:39.520
Let's go, Kisugi!

19:39.520 --> 19:40.490
Yeah!

19:44.990 --> 19:46.500
We're attacking, guys!

19:46.500 --> 19:48.330
We'll get the lead once again.

19:48.330 --> 19:49.120
Yeah.

19:50.160 --> 19:53.710
Let's go! A good offense can be the best defense!

19:53.710 --> 19:56.320
If Tsubasa comes attacking, the ball as good as ours!

19:56.320 --> 19:58.740
Just quickly get the ball and send it to Nitta!

19:58.740 --> 19:59.710
Yeah!

19:59.710 --> 20:00.800
Let's go, Izawa!

20:00.800 --> 20:01.800
Kisugi!

20:01.800 --> 20:02.800
Taki!

20:02.800 --> 20:06.010
We've got a good attacking formation in the second half.

20:06.010 --> 20:10.060
We'll break through the Otomo Quartet this time!

20:10.060 --> 20:12.680
<i>As one would expect, when Tsubasa joins the attack,</i>

20:12.680 --> 20:18.150
<i>Izawa, Kisugi and Taki, who are already skilled to begin with, can move around freely.</i>

20:18.150 --> 20:21.400
Damn it! We easily could get the ball from them until now!

20:21.400 --> 20:24.030
Great! Otomo's defense is crumbling down!

20:24.030 --> 20:26.220
We'll directly aim for their goal!

20:27.160 --> 20:29.840
Yeah, we'll pretend to do so... but pass the ball!

20:30.540 --> 20:31.250
What?!

20:31.250 --> 20:34.200
<i>After breaking their opponent's defense line down,</i>

20:34.200 --> 20:37.250
<i>Nankatsu once more sends to ball to their playmaker, Tsubasa!</i>

20:39.880 --> 20:42.670
<i>Tsubasa sends a direct pass in front of the goal.</i>

20:42.670 --> 20:45.430
<i>After sending that pass, he starts running too!</i>

20:45.430 --> 20:47.180
<i>He makes a pass and go!</i>

20:48.100 --> 20:52.020
<i>Kisugi gets the ball down with his head and sends it to the running Tsubasa.</i>

20:52.540 --> 20:53.520
Oh no!

20:53.920 --> 20:55.230
<i>I'll score.</i>

20:55.230 --> 21:00.030
<i>Even if I'm a midfielder, I'm Nankatsu's playmaker.</i>

21:00.030 --> 21:02.560
<i>I'm also their ace striker!</i>

21:02.560 --> 21:06.530
<i>A true ace striker always turns every single chance into a goal!</i>

21:06.530 --> 21:09.030
Go, Tsubasa!

21:14.980 --> 21:16.440
<i>Goal!</i>

21:16.440 --> 21:18.810
<i>Tsubasa's splendid middle shot!</i>

21:18.810 --> 21:21.960
<i>This time, goalkeeper Ichijo couldn't move a muscle.</i>

21:21.960 --> 21:23.020
All right!

21:23.020 --> 21:25.470
<i>Nankatsu is in the lead with one goal again!</i>

21:25.470 --> 21:28.220
Yes! He did it, he did it, he did it!

21:28.220 --> 21:30.130
You're great!

21:31.600 --> 21:33.020
Sanae...

21:36.760 --> 21:39.650
I-I can't shake that old habit of mine off.

21:39.650 --> 21:42.900
Great, great, Tsubasa!

21:43.330 --> 21:48.010
<i>Otomo Middle School really shouldn't have let this boy take a shot!</i>

21:48.010 --> 21:53.330
<i>Tsubasa changed positions to midfielder in middle school after being</i>

21:53.330 --> 21:56.500
<i>a center forward during his elementary school days.</i>

21:56.500 --> 21:58.640
<i>Still, while his number of shots declined,</i>

21:58.640 --> 22:00.780
<i>his accuracy is as high as ever.</i>

22:00.780 --> 22:07.510
<i>In his 3rd year of participation in this tournament, he actually boasts a 87% rate of his shots becoming goals!</i>

22:07.510 --> 22:09.600
Guys, don't let your guard down.

22:09.600 --> 22:12.640
This one goal was important, but it's still a single goal lead.

22:12.640 --> 22:14.320
We'll keep on protecting it!

22:14.320 --> 22:15.640
Yeah!

22:38.870 --> 22:44.920
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.870 --> 22:44.920
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.920 --> 22:50.930
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.920 --> 22:50.930
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.930 --> 22:56.980
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.930 --> 22:56.980
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.980 --> 23:01.610
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.980 --> 23:01.610
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:07.900
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.230 --> 23:07.900
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.330
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.240 --> 23:15.330
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.330 --> 23:21.370
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.370 --> 23:25.840
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.370 --> 23:25.840
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.130 --> 23:33.470
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.130 --> 23:33.470
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.470 --> 23:39.520
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.520 --> 23:45.820
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.520 --> 23:45.820
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:50.150 --> 24:00.800
COMING UP, EPISODE 32:
OVERTHROW TSUBASA! HYUGA VS. MISUGI
